  "bug": {
    "bug_id": "Jsoup-35",
    "project": "Jsoup",
    "summary": "No title",
    "description": "Using JSoup inclusive the last release 1.7.2 there is a bug parsing HTML with unclosed tags.\n\nExample:\n\nString\n\ntmp\n= \n\"<a href='www.google.com'>Link<p>Error link</a>\"\n;\n\nJsoup\n.\nparse\n(\ntmp\n);\n\nThe Document that generate is:\n\n<\nhtml\n>\n\n<\nhead\n>\n</\nhead\n>\n\n<\nbody\n>\n\n<\na\n\nhref\n=\"\nwww.google.com\n\"\n>\nLink\n</\na\n>\n\n<\np\n>\n<\na\n>\nError link\n</\na\n>\n</\np\n>\n\n</\nbody\n>\n\n</\nhtml\n>\n\nThe browsers would generate something as:\n\n<\nhtml\n>\n\n<\nhead\n>\n</\nhead\n>\n\n<\nbody\n>\n\n<\na\n\nhref\n=\"\nwww.google.com\n\"\n>\nLink\n</\na\n>\n\n<\np\n>\n<\na\n\nhref\n=\"\nwww.google.com\n\"\n>\nError link\n</\na\n>\n</\np\n>\n\n</\nbody\n>\n\n</\nhtml\n>\n\nJsoup should works as browsers or as source code.\n\nAlso there is a question on stackoverflow:\n\nhttp://stackoverflow.com/questions/15813821/jsoup-parsing-unclosed-tags"
  },
